  "body": "Porting from:\r\n\r\n- https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=27314\r\n- https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=26783\r\n\r\nwhich involved @bzbarsky, @nox, and @hsivonen.\r\n\r\nThis is about https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#html-fragment-parsing-algorithm\r\n\r\nI'm not sure I fully understand these threads, but overall it seems like the spec's current mechanisms of \"adjusted current node\" and the fictional start tag token created in step 9 are confusing and don't match natural implementation strategies.\r\n\r\nThe most concrete proposed fix is at https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=26783#c6 . However, I don't feel like I understand the motivating issues enough, or the current spec text's details enough, to evaluate or implement such a fix. If someone (perhaps from the above-mentioned folks, or @zcorpan?) wants to submit a pull request, I can do my best to review!",
